        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "b3rpb",
          "name": "Responsive behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Desktop 1024–1920: fill the main area beside the 236 px sidebar with 46 px gutters, matching Progress. Group surfaces stretch while expanded prose stays within 760 px. Tablet 820: 36 px gutters and the horizontal download row. Mobile 390 and narrow 320: 20 px gutters and a full-width download button above its helper. At zoom or long translations, stack the row before text truncates. Keep the download in normal flow above the drawers, clear of fixed navigation.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "of7Yk",
          "name": "Keyboard and pointer behavior",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Tab order: download, then group headers. Enter or Space starts the download. Keep focus on the control during preparation and after feedback; do not focus the status text. Give the control its visible localized name and associate the contents/language hint. Use the existing hover/pressed treatment and a 2 px focus ring with clear separation. No hover-only information; a static hourglass also works with reduced motion.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "N8EGhQ",
          "name": "Review and assumptions",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Design decisions: download all groups in the current language; one action without a modal; inline feedback; 48 px control height; print-friendly PDF; suggested language-specific filename; 15-second long-wait notice and 60-second recovery. Check render, wrapping, contrast, targets and all 14 retained drawers. Static designs specify browser and assistive-technology behavior; implementation and physical-device verification are still required.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
